/// Reading and changing the system's settings, for the Settings app (P4 task 7).
/// Like `kai:edit`, this is a granted interface, not part of `kai:app` (which is
/// frozen): only an app whose package holds the `settings` grant can import it,
/// and a component that imports it without the grant does not stage
/// (`Reason::Link`). It adds no row for the AI: what a request does is the
/// OS's, not the model's, so the model's view and the typed-only rows stay as
/// they are.
///
/// A request is one line of printable ASCII, `<verb> [<arguments>]`, and is not
/// run inside the call that makes it: the host sends it after the call and tells
/// the app the answer in a later one. A *read* may be sent at any time. A
/// *change* is passed on only when the call that sent it was started by a real
/// key or click from the person at the desktop, and a call may send one change;
/// a change an app sends from `init`, an answer, a timer or an action the AI
/// synthesised is refused with an error answer, so the AI cannot drive the
/// Settings window into revoking or removing anything.
package kai:settings@0.1.0;

interface settings {
    /// Queues `request` for the system and returns its ticket. The whole request
    /// must be one of these, exactly:
    ///
    /// - reads: `rules`, `grants` (the apps that have effect rows) or `grants <app>` (one
    ///   app's rows, an app being 1 to 24 lowercase letters, digits or `-`),
    ///   `about`, `profiles`, `apps` (the apps that can nap), `file appearance`,
    ///   `file apps` and `file updates` (a settings file's bytes);
    /// - changes, where a name is 1 to 24 printable ASCII bytes with one space
    ///   at most between words:
    ///   - `appearance-set <setting> <value>`, a setting of `theme`, `scale`,
    ///     `text_size`, `token`, `reduced_motion` or `legible`, and a value of
    ///     up to 64 bytes;
    ///   - `profile-set <name>`;
    ///   - `rules-remove <n>` or `rules-remove S<n>`, up to four digits;
    ///   - `grants-revoke <app> <row>` and `grants-restore <app> <row>`, a row
    ///     being a lowercase letter then lowercase letters, digits or `_`, up to
    ///     24 bytes;
    ///   - `keep-running on|off <app>`;
    ///   - `restart-window <start> <end>` (minutes of the day, below 1440 and
    ///     different) or `restart-window off`.
    ///
    /// Refused (the call traps) when `request` is anything else, is longer than
    /// 512 bytes, is not printable ASCII, is a second change in the same call, or
    /// 16 requests are waiting for the host already.
    send: func(request: string) -> u32;
}

/// What the system answered.
interface replies {
    /// The answer to the request with this ticket: text (or a settings file's
    /// bytes, at most 64 KiB) for a read, a line saying what was done for a
    /// change, or why there is none (the system is not running, refused it, or
    /// the request was a change the person did not make; at most 200 printable
    /// ASCII bytes). A ticket is not reused while this instance runs; a new
    /// instance starts again from 0.
    on-reply: func(ticket: u32, outcome: result<list<u8>, string>);
}

/// An app that reads and changes settings: the two halves of the grant.
world settings-access {
    import settings;
    export replies;
}
